WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:02.430
- What kind of person make
their own scam business

00:00:02.430 --> 00:00:04.460
and then tricks their
friends into joining?

00:00:04.460 --> 00:00:05.750
How do people fall for something

00:00:05.750 --> 00:00:07.673
that is obviously too good to be true?

00:00:07.680 --> 00:00:09.950
Back in 2012, I got to find out.

00:00:09.950 --> 00:00:12.740
Everything I'm about to
tell you is 100% true

00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:15.763
and filled with a bunch of
bad decisions on my part,

00:00:15.790 --> 00:00:18.280
so I've changed some of
the names and specifics.

00:00:18.280 --> 00:00:19.463
So, here we go.

00:00:21.030 --> 00:00:23.510
I'm 26, working in New
York City, when I get

00:00:23.510 --> 00:00:25.810
a random Facebook message
from a guy named Daniel.

00:00:25.810 --> 00:00:27.530
I've never met him before, but it shows

00:00:27.530 --> 00:00:29.860
we went to the same high
school, so I read his message.

00:00:29.860 --> 00:00:32.420
Hey Jeffrey, I am working
with a local business team

00:00:32.420 --> 00:00:34.253
in online distribution currently.

00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:36.510
We're growing quite a
bit and we're looking for

00:00:36.510 --> 00:00:38.320
one or two ambitious individuals.

00:00:38.320 --> 00:00:40.603
Right off the bat, it
sounded pretty scammy,

00:00:40.720 --> 00:00:42.973
so I told him I was interested.

00:00:43.060 --> 00:00:44.980
On the phone, he tells me he's looking for

00:00:44.980 --> 00:00:47.493
a few go-getters to start
a business of their own.

00:00:47.620 --> 00:00:49.360
He says it would be easy for me,

00:00:49.360 --> 00:00:51.040
I could work in my spare time at home

00:00:51.040 --> 00:00:53.133
as often or as little as I'd like.

00:00:53.220 --> 00:00:55.810
If I was interested, he wanted
me to meet with his boss.

00:00:55.810 --> 00:00:57.290
I had a lot of questions.

00:00:57.290 --> 00:00:59.240
What kind of business was this exactly?

00:00:59.240 --> 00:01:01.460
Uh, my boss can tell you
more when you speak with him.

00:01:01.460 --> 00:01:03.140
And what is the name of your company?

00:01:03.140 --> 00:01:05.240
I'll explain everything
when you meet my boss.

00:01:05.240 --> 00:01:06.940
I've gotten a vague promise of money

00:01:06.940 --> 00:01:09.183
and literally no other information.

00:01:09.460 --> 00:01:10.513
So I tell him I'm in.

00:01:11.440 --> 00:01:13.410
Flash forward to the day of the meeting.

00:01:13.410 --> 00:01:16.270
To prep, I create a fake
resume and put it in a folder

00:01:16.270 --> 00:01:18.700
with a picture of Bill Gates
to really impress them.

00:01:18.700 --> 00:01:21.230
I bought a $20 oversized suit at Goodwill

00:01:21.230 --> 00:01:23.550
along with a pair of bright
yellow running shoes.

00:01:23.550 --> 00:01:25.560
I tell my real coworkers where I'm going

00:01:25.560 --> 00:01:27.575
and that if they don't
hear from me in two hours,

00:01:27.575 --> 00:01:28.733
get worried.

00:01:28.810 --> 00:01:31.360
At the hotel, Daniel is
waiting for me in the lobby

00:01:31.360 --> 00:01:33.933
in a navy blue suit, completely alone.

00:01:34.220 --> 00:01:35.450
Let's go meet everybody.

00:01:35.450 --> 00:01:37.513
Everybody, who is everybody?

00:01:37.600 --> 00:01:39.280
I thought we were just meeting his boss.

00:01:39.280 --> 00:01:41.460
We get into the elevator
and to my surprise,

00:01:41.460 --> 00:01:43.193
Daniel hits the down button.

00:01:43.920 --> 00:01:46.140
Down, what on Earth could be underneath

00:01:46.140 --> 00:01:47.340
the lobby of this hotel?

00:01:47.520 --> 00:01:50.060
For the first time, I start
to get really nervous.

00:01:50.060 --> 00:01:52.723
The doors open and I am stunned.

00:01:53.150 --> 00:01:54.960
We walk into a massive ballroom

00:01:54.960 --> 00:01:57.060
with what's gotta be like 200 people.

00:01:57.060 --> 00:01:58.970
There is a stage with tons of chairs

00:01:58.970 --> 00:02:01.130
and a bunch of other people
wearing the exact same

00:02:01.130 --> 00:02:02.203
navy suit as Daniel.

00:02:02.380 --> 00:02:03.933
I have no idea what's going on.

00:02:03.990 --> 00:02:06.690
Daniel tells me a presentation
will be starting shortly

00:02:06.690 --> 00:02:07.990
and takes me to the seats

00:02:08.010 --> 00:02:09.200
where there's a bunch of other people

00:02:09.200 --> 00:02:11.160
who look like they're in
the same situation as me.

00:02:11.160 --> 00:02:13.370
I immediately turn to the
person sitting next to me

00:02:13.370 --> 00:02:16.030
and ask do you have any
idea what is going on?

00:02:16.030 --> 00:02:18.930
She says she's not sure, it's
just a business opportunity.

00:02:18.960 --> 00:02:20.887
Do you know the person
who invited you here?

00:02:20.887 --> 00:02:22.290
"Not really," she says.

00:02:22.290 --> 00:02:23.800
The person on the other side of me

00:02:23.800 --> 00:02:25.433
says the exact same thing.

00:02:25.830 --> 00:02:27.210
What is going on here?

00:02:27.210 --> 00:02:28.240
Who are these people?

00:02:28.240 --> 00:02:29.720
Why did they come to this event?

00:02:29.720 --> 00:02:31.120
Who in the world would come to this

00:02:31.120 --> 00:02:32.850
with no information at all?

00:02:32.850 --> 00:02:35.730
The lights dim and one of
the navy suits gets on stage

00:02:35.730 --> 00:02:38.633
and tells us we are in for
a very special treat today.

00:02:39.040 --> 00:02:40.910
He introduces a man named Joseph

00:02:41.090 --> 00:02:44.308
and all of the navy suits
erupt into a huge applause,

00:02:44.308 --> 00:02:47.573
cheering and howling like this
man is some kind of a god.

00:02:47.920 --> 00:02:49.900
Joseph walks up to the microphone

00:02:49.900 --> 00:02:52.040
and proceeds to spend the next 15 minutes

00:02:52.040 --> 00:02:54.193
telling us about what a great life he has.

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:57.660
He's 35 years old, his business
is at the diamond level.

00:02:57.660 --> 00:03:01.860
He works three hours a week
and makes $150,000 a year.

00:03:01.860 --> 00:03:03.973
He goes on vacation all the time.

00:03:04.340 --> 00:03:05.700
He's got a beautiful wife.

00:03:05.700 --> 00:03:07.800
He's retiring in the next two years,

00:03:07.800 --> 00:03:10.290
and then he tells us the
most important thing of all.

00:03:10.290 --> 00:03:12.076
This could be all of you.

00:03:12.076 --> 00:03:16.243
Me, me? (gasps)

00:03:16.712 --> 00:03:18.560
He starts pointing to people in the crowd.

00:03:18.560 --> 00:03:21.040
What would you do with
an extra $100 a month?

00:03:21.040 --> 00:03:23.896
What would you do with
an extra $1,000 a month?

00:03:23.896 --> 00:03:26.450
At this point, about
30 minutes have passed

00:03:26.450 --> 00:03:28.070
and the only thing he's
really talked about

00:03:28.070 --> 00:03:29.240
is how good money is

00:03:29.248 --> 00:03:32.030
when he finally tells us
about the opportunity.

00:03:32.030 --> 00:03:33.640
You'd be starting your own business

00:03:33.640 --> 00:03:35.960
that sells home goods and beauty products.

00:03:35.960 --> 00:03:37.930
Instead of going to the store to buy them,

00:03:37.930 --> 00:03:39.180
you'd buy them from yourself.

00:03:39.180 --> 00:03:41.230
Hey, you got some friends who need these?

00:03:41.350 --> 00:03:42.850
They can buy them from you too.

00:03:42.850 --> 00:03:44.850
Why would they support a big corporation

00:03:44.850 --> 00:03:46.400
when they can support a friend?

00:03:47.230 --> 00:03:49.483
If someone you know joins your business,

00:03:49.530 --> 00:03:51.380
you get a percentage
of whatever they make.

00:03:51.380 --> 00:03:54.620
It's easy money, you don't
even have to do anything for.

00:03:54.620 --> 00:03:57.683
Joseph tells us we'll make
the diamond level in no time.

00:03:57.830 --> 00:03:59.303
The audience is eating it up,

00:03:59.340 --> 00:04:00.870
they cannot wait to hear more.

00:04:00.870 --> 00:04:02.560
This sounded like a pyramid scheme to me.

00:04:02.560 --> 00:04:04.700
The sleazeballs at the top of the company

00:04:04.750 --> 00:04:07.270
make a ton of money as
long as a bunch of suckers

00:04:07.270 --> 00:04:08.460
keep signing up below them.

00:04:08.460 --> 00:04:10.990
These unfortunate people will
keep putting their own money

00:04:10.990 --> 00:04:12.790
into this business, losing more money

00:04:12.790 --> 00:04:13.830
than they'll ever make.

00:04:13.830 --> 00:04:16.463
By now, Joseph is wrapping
up his presentation.

00:04:16.550 --> 00:04:18.850
He tells us he knows we're super excited,

00:04:18.850 --> 00:04:20.560
but that we shouldn't
go telling our friends

00:04:20.560 --> 00:04:22.303
or family about anything yet.

00:04:22.430 --> 00:04:24.010
They might have questions
that we don't know

00:04:24.010 --> 00:04:27.100
the answers to and it's
better off if we just wait.

00:04:27.100 --> 00:04:28.760
He says goodbye and the navy suits

00:04:28.760 --> 00:04:30.810
give another excessive round of applause.

00:04:30.846 --> 00:04:34.283
Everyone stands up and Daniel
makes his way back over to me.

00:04:34.370 --> 00:04:36.103
So, what do you think?

00:04:36.220 --> 00:04:38.853
It sounds amazing.

00:04:39.170 --> 00:04:41.690
I can see the dollar signs
light up in his eyes.

00:04:41.690 --> 00:04:42.880
He takes me back to the lobby

00:04:42.880 --> 00:04:45.610
and tells me to hang tight
while he grabs an info packet.

00:04:45.610 --> 00:04:48.440
While I'm waiting there,
I watch as two navy suits

00:04:48.440 --> 00:04:50.280
walk across the entire room

00:04:50.300 --> 00:04:52.120
and stand like two feet away from me.

00:04:52.120 --> 00:04:54.136
So, what level are you at?

00:04:54.136 --> 00:04:56.003
I just got to platinum.

00:04:56.040 --> 00:04:59.410
Wow, and you've only been
doing this for three months.

00:04:59.410 --> 00:05:01.993
And then, they walked away.

00:05:02.473 --> 00:05:04.360
They came across the entire room

00:05:04.360 --> 00:05:05.890
and stood two feet next to me

00:05:05.980 --> 00:05:07.793
just so I could overhear that.

00:05:08.300 --> 00:05:10.733
Daniel returns in gives
me the info packet.

00:05:10.810 --> 00:05:14.053
It's titled Creating Choices,
A Business of Your Own,

00:05:14.220 --> 00:05:16.670
and the very first page
has a picture of a sailboat

00:05:16.670 --> 00:05:18.246
on the ocean with the caption

00:05:18.246 --> 00:05:20.323
imagine where life can take you.

00:05:20.490 --> 00:05:23.440
The book then goes on to a
diagram of their business model,

00:05:23.460 --> 00:05:25.753
which is actually shaped like a pyramid.

00:05:25.850 --> 00:05:27.960
It also shows that the
only thing you need to do

00:05:27.960 --> 00:05:30.590
to start your own business is pay $200

00:05:30.590 --> 00:05:32.053
to get your very own website.

00:05:32.310 --> 00:05:33.680
You gotta pay to play, right?

00:05:33.680 --> 00:05:36.000
He puts the pressure on me to
do it right then and there,

00:05:36.000 --> 00:05:37.910
but I tell him I need
a week to consider it.

00:05:37.910 --> 00:05:40.730
He says "okay," but he warns
me not to google anything

00:05:40.730 --> 00:05:43.320
about the company, so of
course I google the company

00:05:43.320 --> 00:05:46.270
and immediately my browser is
filled with horror stories.

00:05:46.270 --> 00:05:48.720
People talk about losing
their life savings.

00:05:48.720 --> 00:05:50.550
One lady even wrote about her brother

00:05:50.550 --> 00:05:53.263
trying to recruit people
at their father's funeral.

00:05:53.450 --> 00:05:54.683
He was a great man,

00:05:55.460 --> 00:05:57.053
and these are great products.

00:05:58.130 --> 00:05:59.773
Some people call it a cult.

00:05:59.950 --> 00:06:01.410
They brainwash people to convert

00:06:01.410 --> 00:06:03.383
their entire lives to this company.

00:06:03.710 --> 00:06:05.410
They convince you it's not a scam

00:06:05.410 --> 00:06:08.470
and they train you how to reply
to anybody who says it is.

00:06:08.470 --> 00:06:10.320
They have a very special
way they want you to

00:06:10.320 --> 00:06:12.220
run your business, and
it can only be learned

00:06:12.220 --> 00:06:14.350
by purchasing their books and DVDs

00:06:14.460 --> 00:06:16.260
and paying to go to their seminars.

00:06:16.260 --> 00:06:19.103
So it's a week later and I'm
meeting Daniel in a cafe.

00:06:19.360 --> 00:06:22.220
I get a little nervous when he
gets right down to business.

00:06:22.220 --> 00:06:23.990
When I say I don't know
if I'm gonna have enough

00:06:23.990 --> 00:06:26.020
time to do this, you could work as little

00:06:26.020 --> 00:06:27.323
or as much as you like.

00:06:27.490 --> 00:06:29.240
When I say I'm not good at sales,

00:06:29.240 --> 00:06:30.660
we have specialized training

00:06:30.670 --> 00:06:32.590
and we can teach you how to succeed.

00:06:32.590 --> 00:06:35.130
When I say I'm not sure I wanna spend $200

00:06:35.130 --> 00:06:36.130
on something right now,

00:06:36.130 --> 00:06:39.200
actually, the startup fee is $300.

00:06:39.200 --> 00:06:41.480
(record scratches)
Wait wait wait, $300?

00:06:41.480 --> 00:06:43.303
The packet says $200.

00:06:43.350 --> 00:06:47.022
Oh, yes, the $200 starts up your website,

00:06:47.022 --> 00:06:49.390
but there's an extra $100 needed

00:06:49.390 --> 00:06:51.893
to get you your first
training books and videos.

00:06:52.110 --> 00:06:54.023
Eh, I don't think I need those.

00:06:54.310 --> 00:06:56.780
Oh, but it's the only
way our business owners

00:06:56.780 --> 00:06:57.933
can be successful.

00:06:58.060 --> 00:06:59.393
Did you buy them?

00:06:59.550 --> 00:07:00.633
Of course.

00:07:00.870 --> 00:07:01.703
Well,

00:07:02.550 --> 00:07:04.593
then can I just borrow them from you?

00:07:05.130 --> 00:07:05.963
Huh?

00:07:06.430 --> 00:07:08.830
I can see nobody has ever
asked him this before.

00:07:08.910 --> 00:07:10.470
He gets flustered for just a moment,

00:07:10.470 --> 00:07:11.920
but then jumps right back in.

00:07:11.970 --> 00:07:14.480
No, no, no, it's really recommended

00:07:14.480 --> 00:07:15.653
that you buy your own.

00:07:15.870 --> 00:07:16.703
Why?

00:07:16.810 --> 00:07:20.063
Well, if you borrowed mine,
everyone would want to,

00:07:20.080 --> 00:07:22.130
and there wouldn't be enough to go around.

00:07:22.130 --> 00:07:23.700
I tell him I'm a really fast reader

00:07:23.700 --> 00:07:25.350
and I even read most
of of the Harry Potter

00:07:25.350 --> 00:07:26.673
books in a single weekend.

00:07:26.720 --> 00:07:28.120
Are any of your training books

00:07:28.120 --> 00:07:29.670
as long as a Harry Potter book?

00:07:29.670 --> 00:07:30.900
Then it wouldn't really be difficult

00:07:30.900 --> 00:07:32.350
for me to read these quickly.

00:07:32.870 --> 00:07:34.053
Right.

00:07:34.130 --> 00:07:36.293
So, I can just borrow yours?

00:07:36.880 --> 00:07:38.640
And I can't believe it, he says

00:07:39.064 --> 00:07:40.663
I, I guess.

00:07:40.840 --> 00:07:42.830
I'm using logic to get
out of paying him money.

00:07:42.830 --> 00:07:44.600
I can tell that's not what he wants.

00:07:44.600 --> 00:07:46.950
He wants someone who's
not gonna ask questions.

00:07:47.070 --> 00:07:48.820
I could see that for Daniel's sake,

00:07:48.890 --> 00:07:50.290
I should stop wasting his time.

00:07:50.290 --> 00:07:51.830
It's either join his team

00:07:51.946 --> 00:07:53.696
or tell him I was messing with him.

00:07:53.980 --> 00:07:56.243
So I do the only proper thing.

00:07:57.230 --> 00:07:58.363
I abruptly leave.

00:08:00.400 --> 00:08:02.550
Over the next few years,
every now and then,

00:08:02.550 --> 00:08:04.500
I'd get little reminders of this company.

00:08:04.500 --> 00:08:06.140
I actually know someone
else from high school

00:08:06.140 --> 00:08:07.963
who joined and lost a lot of money.

00:08:08.120 --> 00:08:11.070
So after two years, I decide, hey,

00:08:11.070 --> 00:08:12.850
maybe I should check in with Daniel again.

00:08:12.850 --> 00:08:15.173
Hey Daniel, how are
things with the business?

00:08:15.300 --> 00:08:17.300
Did I make a mistake by not joining you?

00:08:17.310 --> 00:08:19.603
Business has been cooking
like never before.

00:08:19.900 --> 00:08:22.860
Well, to tell you the truth,
I can't say you haven't

00:08:22.860 --> 00:08:24.480
missed out, but then again,

00:08:24.480 --> 00:08:27.360
sometimes the timing just
isn't right for people.

00:08:27.360 --> 00:08:29.550
To be honest, I was a little bit surprised

00:08:29.550 --> 00:08:31.260
he was still with the company, but

00:08:31.390 --> 00:08:32.970
I guess that means he was making money.

00:08:32.970 --> 00:08:35.030
I guess it goes to show
you should never give up

00:08:35.030 --> 00:08:38.463
on your dream, even if your
dream is scamming people.

00:08:39.006 --> 00:08:41.923
(triumphant music)

00:08:43.291 --> 00:08:45.874
(upbeat music)

00:08:47.950 --> 00:08:48.873
- [Man] Hey guys, we're--

00:08:48.873 --> 00:08:49.706
- [All] Pero Like!

00:08:49.706 --> 00:08:51.487
- Did you know it's
Hispanic Heritage Month?

00:08:51.491 --> 00:08:52.390
(speaking foreign language)

00:08:52.390 --> 00:08:53.720
- For more Latino content.

00:08:53.720 --> 00:08:54.963
- Subscribe here.

